<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-15 — confirm spaarke-dev runs net10 (runtime + slot evidence)</title>
    <phase>P5 Dev cutover (OPERATOR-DRIVEN)</phase>
    <gate>042 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Evidence-gathering + Azure read commands; operator-driven; no code change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Run az read commands + record; well-specified.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>OPERATOR-DRIVEN — needs Azure credentials; gate for the dev cutover.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>042</deps>
    <tags>deployment, dotnet, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 hour</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>OPERATOR-DRIVEN. Confirm the ONLY active environment — `spaarke-dev` (App Service `spaarke-bff-dev`) — can run .NET 10: run `az webapp list-runtimes --os-type linux` for the dev subscription/region and confirm `DOTNETCORE:10.0` is available, and record whether `spaarke-bff-dev` has a deployment slot (informs whether task 051 does a direct deploy or a slot deploy). NOTE: demo/trial + production are decommissioned for budget — there is NO production cutover in scope now (see the parked tasks 060/061); this evidence is for the dev deploy only.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE release engineer + platform developer. Expert in Azure App Service runtimes, deployment slots, and az CLI. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`notes/dev-runtime-evidence.md` contains the pasted `az webapp list-runtimes` output confirming `DOTNETCORE:10.0` availability for `spaarke-dev`, plus whether `spaarke-bff-dev` has a slot — resolving the runtime-availability open question for the dev deploy.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Environment reality (owner 2026-08-11): only `spaarke-dev` is live; demo/trial + production are decommissioned for budget until a first release ships, and will be re-provisioned on .NET 10 later. So the spec's original "prod region / P1v3 slot swap" (FR-16/NFR-04/NFR-06) is DEFERRED (tasks 060/061 parked) and the near-term cutover is a direct deploy to `spaarke-bff-dev`. Design §7 colon form (`DOTNETCORE:10.0`) still applies for `list-runtimes`. This is the first P5 task and a prerequisite to the dev deploy (051). Operator-driven (needs dev-subscription Azure credentials).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/dev-runtime-evidence.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="042" status="pending">Runbook exists (dev direct-deploy section + future prod slot playbook).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">OPERATOR-DRIVEN: requires dev-subscription Azure credentials; do not fabricate output — paste real `az` results. If `DOTNETCORE:10.0` is not available for the dev App Service, STOP (see escalation) rather than proceeding to deploy.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Read-only Azure commands only — no config changes to `spaarke-bff-dev` in this task (the deploy is task 051).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT re-introduce production-cutover steps here — production is decommissioned; the prod slot-swap procedure lives in the task-042 runbook as a FUTURE playbook.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Azure runtime availability + slot verification (dev)</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="list-runtimes" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §7 — verify runtime with `az webapp list-runtimes --os-type linux` (colon form).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-15 + the environment-reality note. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD. Confirm operator + dev Azure auth.</step>
    <step order="1">Run `az webapp list-runtimes --os-type linux`; capture the output; confirm `DOTNETCORE:10.0` present.</step>
    <step order="2">Check whether `spaarke-bff-dev` has a deployment slot (`az webapp deployment slot list`); record the result (drives direct-vs-slot deploy in 051).</step>
    <step order="3">Write `notes/dev-runtime-evidence.md` with the pasted evidence.</step>
    <step order="4">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 050 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If `DOTNETCORE:10.0` is NOT available for the dev App Service, STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT reach for a self-contained-publish escape hatch (spec MUST NOT); this is a go/no-go input for the dev deploy.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">n/a (az CLI)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/dev-runtime-evidence.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/dev-runtime-evidence.md` contains real `az webapp list-runtimes` output confirming `DOTNETCORE:10.0` availability for the dev environment.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Whether `spaarke-bff-dev` has a deployment slot is recorded (drives 051's direct-vs-slot deploy).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if the runtime is absent, the task STOPPED and escalated (no self-contained workaround).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no production-cutover step is present (production is out of scope; prod procedure stays in the 042 runbook as a future playbook).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-15 (evidence half), reframed for dev-only environment reality (owner 2026-08-11). OPERATOR-DRIVEN. Original "prod region/slot" framing is deferred with tasks 060/061.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
